{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>עלי באר.</b> From within the wadi — and bring up what you bring up. And from where do we know that the well announced itself to them? For it is said ״וּמִשָּׁם בְּאֵרָה״ — was it then from there? Was it not with them from the start of the forty years? Rather, it descended to publicize the miracles (Tanchuma). And so too ״אָז יָשִׁיר״ — this song was said at the end of forty, and the well was given to them at the start of forty. What did He see to write it here? Rather, this matter is expounded above, from it."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:58.023306932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}